--TEST--
`Core\Test::sentHttp` hands back every outbound call the program made, in order, and nothing a record reads is `tainted` — `rule:testing/an-outbound-call-is-answered-from-a-table`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The claim is *invariance over a sweep*: four calls differing in verb, URL and
// headers, asserted by walking the records rather than by reading one of them,
// so a table that answered each call plausibly and recorded the wrong one still
// fails here.

Core\Test::answerHttp("https://api.example.com/*", 200, {body: "ok"});

var $a = Core\Http\Client::get("https://api.example.com/users/1", {headers: ["Authorization" => "Bearer one"]});
var $b = Core\Http\Client::post("https://api.example.com/users", {headers: ["Content-Type" => "application/json"]});
var $c = Core\Http\Client::delete("https://api.example.com/users/1");
// An unanswered call is a call the program made, so it is recorded before the
// table is asked whether it knows the URL.
try {
    var $d = Core\Http\Client::put("https://other.example.com/users/1");
} catch (LogicError $unmatched) {
    echo "refused", "\n";
}

var $sent = Core\Test::sentHttp();
echo Core\Arr::count($sent), "\n";
foreach ($sent as Core\Test\SentRequest $call) {
    // A header name is case-insensitive, so the name a test asks under is not
    // the name the subject happened to write.
    echo ($call->method() as int), " ", $call->url(),
         " auth=", $call->header("AUTHORIZATION") ?? "-",
         " type=", $call->header("content-type") ?? "-",
         " body=", Core\Bytes::length($call->body()), "\n";
}

// Nothing on a record is `tainted`: a URL read back out of one is accepted at
// `rule:security/outbound-url-is-a-sink`'s sink, which is the position that
// refuses a value that came from outside. A reply's `text()` in this position
// is a compile-time diagnostic, and that asymmetry is the rule's own last
// paragraph.
foreach ($sent as Core\Test\SentRequest $call) {
    if ($call->url() != "https://other.example.com/users/1") {
        var $echoed = Core\Http\Client::head($call->url());
        echo $echoed->status(), "\n";
    }
}
--EXPECT--
refused
4
0 https://api.example.com/users/1 auth=Bearer one type=- body=0
4 https://api.example.com/users auth=- type=application/json body=0
7 https://api.example.com/users/1 auth=- type=- body=0
5 https://other.example.com/users/1 auth=- type=- body=0
200
200
200
